  "job_B3.2.2_20251003_114620": {
    "text": "Omelia epyffania domini.\nMen \u00fea leofestan, sceolon we nu hwylcumhwegu wordum secgan be \u00f0\u00e6re arweor\u00f0nesse \u00feysse halgan\n\u00d0\u00e6t w\u00e6s on \u00feyssum d\u00e6ge \u00fee nu andweard is \u00f0\u00e6t ure dryhten gefulwad wolde bion.\nNe dyde for \u00f0y \u00fee him \u00e6fre \u00e6nig synn o\u00f0\u00f0e leahtor on him w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t him sceolde fulwihtes b\u00e6\u00f0\nFor \u00f0an s\u00e6g\u00f0 sanctus M\u00e6theus se godspellere \u00f0as dryhtenlican fulwihtes d\u00e6g \u00e6fter \u00feysse\nIohannes autem prohibebat eum dicens Iohannes him \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a bewerede & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Hw\u00e6t, \u00f0\u00e6t is\nRespondit autem Iesus et dixit.\n\u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6ter \u00e6t \u00f0am fulwihte gecl\u00e6nsode o\u00f0\u00fee him \u00f0\u00e6s \u00e6nig \u00feearf w\u00e6re, ac he eall w\u00e6ter \u00feurh hine\n& he on him gefulwad w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t hie a sie\u00f0\u00f0an meahton \u00feurh gastlice halgunge mancynn Gode sylfum to\n& swa bi\u00f0 \u00e6ghwylc \u00fe\u00e6ra manna se \u00f0e rihtlice bi\u00f0 gefulwad, he bi\u00f0 Godes bearn gif he \u00feonne \u00f0a\n& he swa cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Iohannes him andswerede & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6t w\u00e6re gedafenlicre \u00fe\u00e6t Crist\nEfne swa swa he cw\u00e6de: Ic eom deadlic mann & gehrorenlic, & \u00feurh Adames scylde ic eom\n& \u00f0a andswarode him sanctus Iohannes & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ac nis \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6s fulwihtes b\u00e6\u00f0 nan \u00feearf, for \u00fean\nac ne m\u00e6g \u00e6nig man \u00feine cl\u00e6nnesse ne \u00feine halignesse geiecan, ac \u00e6lc man sceal \u00feurh \u00fee bion cl\u00e6ne\nSe h\u00e6lend him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Forl\u00e6t \u00feis bion nesse \u00fe\u00e6t wit mancynne eallre h\u00e6lo & ealre eadmodnesse\nSwa swa he to \u00f0am on middangeard cwom \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feurh hine gefylled w\u00e6re & \u00fe\u00e6t he\n& rihtlice \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s, \u00fe\u00e6t dryhten geteohhod h\u00e6fde, \u00fe\u00e6t seo ece h\u00e6lo to mancynne \u00feurh fulwihte\nSe h\u00e6lend \u00fea andswarode Iohanne & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: \u00fe\u00e6t me gedafena\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ic ealle so\u00f0f\u00e6stnesse gefylle.\n& \u00fea forlet he \u00feone h\u00e6lend under his handa & hine \u00fea gefulwade.\nFor \u00f0an \u00fee se eadiga wer sanctus Iohannes, \u00e6rest he wi\u00f0cw\u00e6\u00f0, for \u00fean he cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t he forhtode\n& sanctus Iohannes, he h\u00e6fde egesan to \u00fean, & him \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feuhte \u00fe\u00e6t his gemet ne w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t se heofonlica\nFor \u00fean he \u00fe\u00e6t dyde for his eadmodnesse, he \u00e6rest wi\u00f0cw\u00e6\u00f0, ac \u00f0onne mid hyrsumnesse he ge\u00f0afode.\nSwylce wear\u00f0 \u00e6t \u00feam dryhtenlican fulwihte se cwide & se witedom gefylled & geworden \u00fee Dauid se\nHe \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0: Quid est tibi mare quod fugisti? & tu Iordanis quare conuersus es restrorsum? Hw\u00e6t is\nIordan is haten seo ea \u00fee se h\u00e6lend on gefulwad w\u00e6s, & heo is swi\u00f0e mycel w\u00e6ter & swi\u00f0e strang\n& \u00fea w\u00e6s geworden in \u00fea tid \u00fee se h\u00e6lend in \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6ter astag \u00fea gecyrde se s\u00e6flod & se stream eall on\nOngeat sio gesceaft \u00fe\u00e6s scyppendes mihta \u00fea sona \u00feurh hire gecynd, swa swa ealle gesceafta \u00feone\nHw\u00e6t, hine \u00e6rest heofonas ongeaton, & for \u00fean sona heora steorran to tacne sendon \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0a\nHw\u00e6t, hine eac swylce s\u00e6 & eall w\u00e6tercynn ongeaton, & hie for \u00fean under his fotum geheardedon &\n& swa we leornia\u00f0 on godspellum \u00fe\u00e6t he ofer \u00feone s\u00e6 & ofer w\u00e6ter mid his fotum eode to his\n& swylce eac \u00e6t \u00feyssum fulwihte \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6ter hine ongeat & ondette, & se stream eall on b\u00e6cling\nSwylce eac \u00feeos eor\u00f0e hine ongeat, & heo for \u00f0an bifode & geforhtode in \u00fea tid \u00fee he for mannum\n& hw\u00e6t, hine eac swylce wegas & stanas ongeaton, & swa we leornia\u00fe on bocum \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a w\u00e6s\nHw\u00e6t, hine eac seo hel sylfa ongeat, for \u00f0an \u00fee heo \u00e6r deade geh\u00e6fte on hire h\u00e6fde, & \u00fea heo eft \u00feurh\n& swa ure dryhten hine ealle o\u00f0re gesceafta ongeaton & ondettan.\n& hine \u00feonne hw\u00e6\u00f0re \u00f0a forheardydan heortan Iudeas hine ne woldon ongitan, ac hie w\u00e6ron heardran\nAc for \u00fean we \u00fe\u00e6s sceolon, men \u00fea leofestan, urum dryhtne a singalice mid eallre heortan \u00feancian \u00fe\u00e6s\nSceolon we nu eac, bro\u00f0or mine, \u00feone halgan godspell secgan & reccan \u00fe\u00e6t we \u00e6r ongunnon secgan.\n& he swa cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Crist, \u00fea he w\u00e6s gefullad, \u00fea astah he of \u00feam w\u00e6tere, & him \u00fea w\u00e6ron heofonas\nSe godspellere, for \u00f0an he swa cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Criste heofonas opene w\u00e6ron, & ealle gesceafta, \u00e6g\u00f0er ge\nAc mid gastlicum eagum & \u00feurh gastlice gesyh\u00f0e \u00feas heofonas w\u00e6ron geopenode, & he mid \u00fey\nHe \u00f0a, sanctus Iohannes, geseah Godes gast of heofonum astigende, on culfran onsyne ofer hine\nCulfre bi\u00f0 bi\u00f0 witre gecynde, for \u00fean se halga gast on culfran onsyne ofer Crist cumende w\u00e6s \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re\nSwa se witiga be \u00f0an to dryhtene cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic wat, dryten, \u00f0\u00e6t \u00f0u eart ge\u00feyldig & ea\u00femod & swi\u00f0e\n& \u00fea w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s heahf\u00e6deres stefn geworden of heofonum & seo w\u00e6s sprecende & \u00feus cwe\u00f0ende: \u00feis\nEfne swa he cw\u00e6de: \u00feis me is gecyndelic sunu.\nIn manegum stowum we \u00fe\u00e6t leornia\u00fe, in conone \u00fe\u00e6re boc & in o\u00f0rum Godes bocum, \u00fe\u00e6t ure dryhten\nAc seo syb bi\u00f0 hw\u00e6\u00f0re \u00feurh dryhtnes gife & \u00feurh his mildheortnesse.\n& nu ure dryhten, h\u00e6lenda Crist, he w\u00e6s \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan God f\u00e6der gecyndelic sunu, for \u00fean \u00fee he\nBro\u00f0or mine, us is \u00feonne nu mycel neod\u00feearf \u00fe\u00e6t we geleornian Godes geleafan swa us riht sie & we\nBro\u00f0or mine, ic ne wat butan hwylc man sie se \u00f0e ungel\u00e6redra sy & he \u00feus on his modge\u00feanc & on\nOn \u00feam is ge\u00feoht swylcum manna, anra gehwylc m\u00e6g him sylfa geandswerian.\nHw\u00e6t, we feala \u00feinga geseo\u00f0 on \u00feyssum woruldlicum gesceaftum \u00f0\u00e6t is an \u00feing & hw\u00e6\u00f0re \u00f0reo \u00feing\n\u00feeah \u00f0e seo gesceaft ne sie gelic to metenne wi\u00f0 \u00feam scippende ne \u00fe\u00e6t lytle \u00feing wi\u00f0 \u00f0am m\u00e6stan, ac\nHw\u00e6t, we geseo\u00f0 \u00feonne gearlice \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feis fyr \u00fee her man beforan us hafa\u00f0, hw\u00e6t, \u00fe\u00e6t is an leg, &\nHe hafa\u00f0 \u00e6rest his sylfes onsyne \u00fe\u00e6t he is hat, & \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00f0er \u00fe\u00e6t he is hwit, swa we geseon\n& \u00feonne is hit hw\u00e6\u00f0re an leg, & ne m\u00e6g \u00e6nig man \u00fe\u00e6t hate fram \u00f0am hwite ascadan ne \u00f0\u00e6t hwite\nAc \u00fe\u00e6t is an fyr swa we geseo\u00f0, & nu swa \u00feonne seo halige \u00ferynis, f\u00e6der & sunu & se haliga gast,\n& he nu eallra wealde\u00f0 a to widan feore, for \u00f0an \u00fee his rices & his mihta n\u00e6fre \u00e6nig ende cyme\u00f0.\n& ealle \u00fea men \u00fea \u00fee nu her in worulde synd, so\u00f0 & riht don willa\u00f0 & on his bebodu a wunia\u00f0, ealle\n& nu, bro\u00f0or mine, \u00fe\u00e6t f\u00e6gere rice & \u00fea eadignesse & \u00f0a myclan wyr\u00f0mendo we sculon nu\nSwa se apostol be \u00f0an cw\u00e6\u00f0: Per multas tribulationes oportet nos intrare in regnum Dei. \u00feurh\nAc utan we gemunan hu ure yldran, \u00fea \u00e6restan men, \u00feurh hwylc \u00feing hie \u00f0a eadelican life forworhton\nEfene hie w\u00e6ron \u00feurh oferhygdnesse, & \u00feurh ungehyrsumnesse & \u00feurh \u00fea lufan \u00fe\u00e6s idlan wuldres &\n& nu se man se \u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feence\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he of \u00feysse gehrorenlican worulde \u00feone heofonlican rice begite, he\nHe sceal beon \u00feonne ea\u00f0mod on his heortan & hersum to \u00e6lcum men & to Gode, & he sceal \u00feysse\nEfne he sceal eac \u00fea lufian for Godes naman \u00fea \u00fee him wi\u00f0erwearde synd, & he sceal halige w\u00e6ccan\nHe sceal f\u00e6sten begangan & \u00fea lufian mid cl\u00e6ne \u00e6lmessan & mid mycle forwyr\u00f0nesse habban on his\n& he sceall beon \u00e6lmesgeorn for Godes naman & for his sawle.\n\u00feurh \u00feas lare, bro\u00f0or mine, & \u00feurh \u00f0as d\u00e6da, \u00fea \u00fee ure m\u00e6ssepreostas us t\u00e6ca\u00fe & l\u00e6ra\u00f0, \u00feonne\nAc uton we nu for \u00fean, men \u00fea leofestan, ure sylfra lif mid mycle egesan & mid mycle behygdnesse\n& mid \u00feyllicum d\u00e6dum we magon \u00fea heofonlican rice begitan & on becuman, mid urne dryhten,",
